1
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:04,560
Okay, the next section of your text deals with the vagina.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:09,100
Recall that the vagina is a fibromuscular canal that leads to the cervix,

3
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,480
and the first of the disorders that we want to talk about is adenosis.

4
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,080
However, before we can understand adenosis, we need a little bit of background,

5
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:17,700
and so I'm going to take you to the whiteboard.

6
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:21,180
Again, the vagina is a fibromuscular canal,

7
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:25,080
and this fibromuscular canal is lined by surface epithelium,

8
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:28,880
and it so happens that the surface epithelium of this canal

9
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:34,440
is stratified squamous epithelium that is non-keratinizing.

10
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,180
And so what I'm drawing here, each of these boxes represents a squamous cell

11
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,680
that together is forming this stratified squamous epithelium

12
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:43,320
that, again, is non-keratinizing.

13
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,900
Now, this is the normal lining of the vaginal canal.

14
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,660
However, if we go back to embryology,

15
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,840
recall that the vaginal canal is actually derived from two different things.

16
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,000
The lower one-third of the vaginal canal

17
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,540
is derived from something called the urogenital sinus,

18
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,960
and the upper two-thirds of the vaginal canal

19
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,720
is derived from something called the malarian duct.

20
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:08,480
Now, remember that the malarian duct

21
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:11,340
is the source of the female reproductive system.

22
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:14,340
So, for example, the uterus is derived from the malarian duct,

23
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,600
the tubes are derived from the malarian duct,

24
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,900
the cervix is derived from the malarian duct,

25
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,600
and the upper two-thirds of the vagina

26
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,440
is also derived from the malarian duct.

27
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:26,400
Now, let's go back down to this lower one-third urogenital sinus.

28
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:35,480
The cells that line the urogenital sinus are normally stratified squamous epithelium.

29
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:43,460
However, the cells that line the upper two-thirds that was derived from the malarian duct in utero is columnar.

30
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:49,960
And so what happens during development is that the stratified squamous epithelium from the lower one-third

31
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:56,940
begins to extend during development again, all the way up to eventually replace the entire vaginal canal

32
00:01:56,940 --> 00:02:00,480
so that these columnar cells should disappear and be replaced by squamous cells.

33
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:05,600
If there is a disruption of this process and the columnar cells persist,

34
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:11,960
then the presence of persistent columnar epithelium in the vaginal canal is called adenosis.

35
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,320
And that's what I've mentioned here in your text.

36
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:20,520
So adenosis is focal persistence of columnar epithelium in the upper vagina

37
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:24,620
because, of course, the upper vagina is derived from the malarian duct.

38
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,060
Now, this can rarely happen in a normal individual.

39
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:34,580
However, the key association is that adenosis is seen with increased incidence in females

40
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:38,300
that are exposed to a drug called DES in utero,

41
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:42,680
or females that were, I should say, exposed to a drug called DES in utero.

42
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:46,840
Now, DES, we need a little bit of a pharmacology tie-in here.

43
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,680
So DES actually stands for diethylstilbestarol,

44
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:54,060
and it is an estrogen-like compound that was developed in the late 1930s.

45
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,940
It was initially used to treat symptoms of postmenopause,

46
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:01,680
but over time it gained popularity for prevention of pregnancy-related complications.

47
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:06,200
So, for example, women who had miscarriage or who had preterm labor

48
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:10,360
would be given this drug while they were pregnant.

49
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:13,940
Eventually, we learned that this drug crossed the placenta,

50
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:18,400
and when it crossed the placenta, it would cause disruption of uterine development,

51
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:22,380
and one of the things that it would disrupt was a conversion of columnar epithelium

52
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:25,800
to squamous epithelium in the vaginal canal.

53
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:30,840
So again, remember that the lower one-third, which was derived from the urogenital sinus, was squamous,

54
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:35,480
and the upper two-thirds, which was derived from the malarian duct, was columnar.

55
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,700
And these squamous cells would go up and would normally replace the columnar cells.

56
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:42,320
However, DES would block this process,

57
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:47,560
and women who were exposed to DES in utero when this process was occurring in fetal life

58
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:51,620
would eventually not have this process occur properly,

59
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,980
and so they would have residual columnar cells,

60
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:58,220
and the presence of those residual columnar cells was called adenosis.

61
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,160
Here's an example of a patient with adenosis.

62
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:04,120
Essentially, I'm drawing the basement membrane here,

63
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:09,680
and everything to the left of this basement membrane is stratified squamous epithelium,

64
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,980
and here represents the canal.

65
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,560
So essentially, everything to the left is normal.

66
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:19,400
Now, in this particular woman, as the squamous cells came up and replaced,

67
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,740
the other thing that should have happened is that the columnar cells

68
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:27,400
that were present deep underneath the epithelium, within the canal itself,

69
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,200
should also have been resorbed.

70
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:34,500
And in this particular case, which these cells again here that I'm circling should have been resorbed.

71
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:38,020
However, in this particular case, these cells are not resorbed,

72
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:42,500
and so you have persistence of columnar epithelium in the upper two-thirds of the vaginal canal.

73
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,520
Now, you wouldn't know that this is the upper two-thirds.

74
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,540
I'd have to tell you that.

75
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:47,760
But in the upper two-thirds of the vaginal canal,

76
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:53,480
and so it's this persistence of columnar epithelium that again refers to adenosis,

77
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:57,860
and this picture is actually taken from a woman who was exposed to DES in utero.

78
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:00,420
Now, adenosis wouldn't be that big of an issue,

79
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:03,480
but the key problem is that adenosis can lead to another complication,

80
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,400
which is called clear-cell adenocarcinoma.

81
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:09,820
Carcinoma, of course, refers to a malignant proliferation of cells.

82
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,320
Adeno refers to the fact that those cells are forming glands,

83
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:16,480
and clear-cell tells us that they have a clear cytoplasm.

84
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:22,460
And so, essentially, the complication of adenosis is that women could develop later on in life

85
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,420
clear-cell adenocarcinoma.

86
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:29,480
And this is a rare complication of DES-associated vaginal adenosis.

87
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:34,560
Now, it was the discovery of clear-cell adenocarcinoma,

88
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,960
along with other complications that eventually led to the cessation of DES usage,

89
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:43,880
and ever since about the late 1970s, we no longer used this drug.

90
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:47,140
I'd like to briefly just talk about some of these other complications,

91
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:50,020
because it is important to know.

92
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:54,480
And so, let's just kind of review the patient populations that could be exposed to DES.

93
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:58,940
So, the first patient population that could be exposed would be a DES mom.

94
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:02,640
So, this is a mother who was pregnant, let's say, in the 60s,

95
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,960
and she had some preterm labor, and so she was exposed to DES.

96
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,660
Now, if DES mom was carrying a girl,

97
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,420
then the drug would cross the placenta,

98
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:13,440
and she would produce a DES daughter.

99
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:19,580
And if a DES mom was carrying a boy,

100
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,280
then the drug would cross the placenta,

101
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,180
and it would produce a DES son.

102
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:27,080
So, these are kind of the key populations that could be exposed to DES.

103
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,960
Now, DES daughters, the key first complication,

104
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:31,960
which we've already discussed,

105
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,040
is that they could get vaginal adenosis.

106
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:39,480
And the problem with adenosis is that that adenosis could potentially become

107
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:43,120
something called clear cell adenal carcinoma,

108
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:46,080
which was the feared complication of exposure to DES.

109
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,380
Another thing that could happen in a DES daughter

110
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:54,420
is that there could be abnormalities of just the formation of the uterus and the tubes,

111
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:58,120
in particular, the smooth muscle of the uterus and the tubes.

112
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:02,760
And so, they would get abnormalities in the formation of the uterus in relation to the tubes.

113
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:09,380
And this could lead to an increased risk of ectopic pregnancy, infertility, or pregnancy loss.

114
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,520
So, pregnancy and gestational type problems.

115
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:16,600
So, those are the two major complications that would arise in DES daughters.

116
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,880
Now, DES sons, fortunately, they have no significant complications.

117
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:25,380
Now, DES moms, the one key complication that I would point out,

118
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:29,600
is that DES moms, or mothers who were exposed to DES when they were pregnant,

119
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,980
have a slightly increased risk for breast carcinoma.

120
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,320
And that shouldn't be hard to remember,

121
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:41,360
because DES essentially was an estrogen-derived compound.

122
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:46,280
And breast carcinoma is something that is related to estrogen exposure.

123
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:51,640
And so, it's not hard to associate the exposure of an estrogen-like compound

124
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:54,560
with a cancer that's related to exposure to estrogen.

125
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,320
And so, those are the key patient populations that would be exposed to DES.

126
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:00,060
And those are the key complications.

127
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:04,740
And it's the learning of all of this that led to the cessation, again,

128
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:06,980
of the use of the drug, and it's no longer in use.

129
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:10,040
The second disorder that we want to talk about

130
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,600
is something called embrinal rhabdomyosarcoma.

131
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:16,620
Sarcoma refers to a malignant mesenchymal proliferation.

132
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:23,620
And rhabdomyo refers to a cell that has features of skeletal muscle.

133
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:28,380
And so, this is a malignant proliferation of immature skeletal muscle.

134
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:31,060
It's relatively rare.

135
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:34,140
I highly doubt you'll ever see one in your practice.

136
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:38,020
However, those things that are rare in practice are often common on exams,

137
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:40,720
and so, it's important to be aware of this disorder.

138
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:46,840
Now, this disorder has a very interesting presentation that you need to be aware of.

139
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:50,760
And that is that this disorder often presents with bleeding

140
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:57,460
and a grape-like mass, which is arising from the vagina, if it's a female,

141
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,760
or the penis, if it's a male.

142
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:04,020
And it classically occurs in a child less than five years of age.

143
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:07,120
Because this produces this grape-like mass,

144
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,820
now, it's also called sarcoma botrydes,

145
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,540
and botrydes refers to grape-like mass,

146
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,940
or it's a term that literally means grape-like mass.

147
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,540
Here's a picture of the grape-like mass,

148
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,360
and all I'm showing you here is the mass.

149
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:21,720
I'm not showing you, obviously, the protrusion of the mass

150
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:23,260
from the vagina or the penis.

151
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:26,940
But essentially, you notice all these grape-like bubbles,

152
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:28,700
or grape-like protrusions here.

153
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:32,260
And so, they call this sarcoma botrydes,

154
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:34,720
again, because of the grape-like mass,

155
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:38,500
and it also, of course, represents an embryonorhabdomyosarcoma.

156
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:41,080
Now, they don't usually show this picture on exams,

157
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,880
but they often show a picture of a five-year-old girl,

158
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,020
which is the classic picture,

159
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,580
and they show this mass protruding from the vagina,

160
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,480
and so that would be the classic presentation.

161
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,120
Embryonorhabdomyosarcoma has a key cell,

162
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:54,660
which forms the tumor,

163
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:57,400
and that cell is called a rhabdomyoblast.

164
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:00,360
The rhabdomyo, again, refers to skeletal muscle,

165
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:03,540
and the blast refers to the fact that it is an immature cell.

166
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:06,820
So, rhabdomyosarcoma is actually defined

167
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,120
by the presence of rhabdomyoblast,

168
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:10,480
and that's an important take-home here.

169
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:14,340
Now, a couple of features of the rhabdomyoblast

170
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:15,320
that we should be aware of.

171
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,520
The first is that rhabdomyoblast

172
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,860
will often show cytoplasmic cross-driation.

173
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,980
So, when you look at a rhabdomyoblast,

174
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,240
and you look at the cytoplasm,

175
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:28,080
you'll often see these cross-driations running up and down the cytoplasm,

176
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,900
similar to what you would see in skeletal muscle.

177
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,820
And so, if I were to tell you, for example,

178
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,860
that there is a child, and they have a tumor,

179
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:39,280
and the pathologist says that the tumor exhibits cytoplasmic cross-driations,

180
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,020
you're going to think about a rhabdomyoblast,

181
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,640
and in turn, a rhabdomyosarcoma.

182
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:47,880
Another way by which we can define the rhabdomyoblast,

183
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:50,500
or maybe I should say identify the rhabdomyoblast,

184
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,900
is to use something called immunohistochemistry.

185
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,800
Now, we can stain for certain antigens present in the cell,

186
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:58,820
which would then help us to identify the cell.

187
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:01,180
And two of the key antigens that are helpful

188
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:03,120
in identifying a rhabdomyoblast

189
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,380
are desmin and myogenin.

190
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,360
Desmin, again, is the intermediate filament

191
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:12,240
that is present in muscle cells.

192
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:15,480
And so, if we know that a cell is positive for desmin,

193
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,540
we know that it is a muscle cell.

194
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:22,040
And myogenin is a nuclear transcription factor

195
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,960
that would be present in immature skeletal muscle.

196
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,640
And so, if the tumor is positive for desmin and myogenin,

197
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:30,120
that would automatically tell us

198
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,400
that we're dealing with muscle

199
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,780
that is immature skeletal muscle,

200
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:36,240
and of course, because it's producing a mass or a tumor,

201
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:39,320
that would indicate a rhabdomyosarcoma.

202
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,040
And so, these are some important features

203
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:43,200
of rhabdomyosarcoma that we should be aware of.

204
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:46,440
The final disorder that we're going to talk about

205
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,760
is vaginal carcinoma.

206
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:49,840
Vaginal carcinoma is a carcinoma

207
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,140
that arises from the squamous epithelium

208
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:53,800
that lines the vaginal mucosa.

209
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:57,000
I've already told you that the entire vaginal mucosa

210
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,900
is lined by squamous epithelium.

211
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:02,360
This tumor is classically related to high-risk HPV,

212
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:07,400
so you're thinking about HPV 16, 18, 31, and 33.

213
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:11,800
And the precursor lesion for this is dysplasia,

214
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:16,760
which, again, is called the vaginal intraepithelial neoplasia,

215
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:20,360
also called the VAIN.

216
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:25,860
And that, again, is the dysplastic precursor

217
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,940
from high-risk HPV,

218
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,760
which eventually becomes vaginal carcinoma.

219
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:32,440
Now, one important thing to note

220
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,380
is that patients who get vaginal carcinoma

221
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,840
that eventually invades and spreads

222
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,480
will get spread to regional lymph nodes

223
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:42,760
as, again, carcinomas generally go to regional lymph nodes.

224
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,640
But what you need to know

225
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:46,340
and what's particularly high-yield here

226
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:49,660
is that because the vagina is derived

227
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,880
from two different sources,

228
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,620
depending on where the cancer is,

229
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:55,160
the spread will be to two different sets of lymph nodes.

230
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,140
So recall, again, that the vagina,

231
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,380
the lower one-third,

232
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,760
is derived from something called the urogenital sinus.

233
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:05,240
And so cancers that arise from the lower one-third

234
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:08,120
will actually spread to the inguinal nodes.

235
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:12,660
Recall, again, that the upper two-thirds of the vagina

236
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:14,760
is derived from the malarian duct.

237
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:17,080
And so cancers from the upper two-thirds

238
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:20,240
will actually spread to the regional iliac nodes.

239
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,260
And this is, again, particularly high-yield

240
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,020
because it's a nice way that examiners

241
00:13:24,020 --> 00:13:26,240
can go back to basic anatomy

242
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:29,020
and test you on relationship of embryology

